Ladybird ends an iframe focus request when its local navigable has
no active document. Blink’s HTMLFrameElementBase::SetFocused checks
ContentFrame() before passing it to FocusController::SetFocusedFrame.
WebKit checks contentFrame() in HTMLFrameElementBase::setFocus. Gecko
resolves the subdocument and its window in nsFocusManager::SetFocusInner
before descending into the child.

Chrome 158.0.8127.36, Firefox 151.0, and WebKit 26.5 all focused a
connected blank iframe and preserved focus on the prior button for
a detached iframe. Chrome and WebKit also preserved it for an inert
iframe. Firefox moved focus in that control. The missing-document case
is the archived Ladybird crash.
